 "gap_notes": [
  "VIX9D is not replicated from the stored chain: no stored Cboe candidate expiries on both sides of 9 days: the nearest pair 2026-12-24 (30.0d) / 2027-01-22 (59.0d) would extrapolate (near weight 1.724, outside [0, 1]), which is not Cboe's interpolation.",
  "The stored chain holds no zero-bid lines (two-sided capture), so Cboe's two-consecutive-zero-bid stop cannot trigger: every stored OTM strike with a bid enters the strip, which can only add variance relative to Cboe's rule on the same book; the stored book's own strike range is the binding limit.",
  "No quote time is stored for this snapshot (Yahoo); the calculation uses 16:00 ET on the session and the official close is the 16:15 ET print (the official index traded 25.98-32.38 that session). Any intraday drift between the snapshot and 16:15 is unmeasured.",
  "near-term 2026-12-24: 115 puts / 100 calls, strip K/F 0.366-1.209",
  "next-term 2027-01-22: 49 puts / 73 calls, strip K/F 0.420-1.289",
  "Model variance swaps at 30 days (k in [-3, 2], wings beyond the fitted K/F 0.70-1.30 extrapolated, so each inherits its model's wing bias): SVI-cal 28.43, SVI 28.41, eSSVI 27.85.",
  "Gap attribution (VIX, SVI-cal surface): replicated - official = +2.85. Strikes beyond the stored strip would add +0.01 under the surface's wing; the stored quotes beyond the fitted K/F 0.70-1.30 are 0.67 index points richer than that wing, so the truncation figure likely understates. Inside the fitted range market and surface differ by +0.12 (these two terms set the replication against the surface; they are not part of the gap). Left unexplained by the chain: -2.86 (official - replicated - truncation; 100% of official - replicated): snapshot timing vs the 16:15 ET print, stale quotes."
